Yes, among others. I noticed some time ago that mithril armor seems to
have this property as well - after checking the source I discovered, that
every armor has, apart from its visible AC, also certain 'cancellation
factor', which is used when computing probability of level drain. 
Most cloaks have quite high cancellation factor, also some types of body 
armour have it. It protects not only from level drains, but also some
other special attack. The protection isn't, however 100% proof - even
with high cancellation there is some chance (around 1%) that you get drained.

So now you know, what unenchanted orcish and dwarvish cloaks are for...
Of course there is a sure way - get Excalibur or Stormy, or polymorph
into something resistant to level drains

